WEBVTT

00:15.390 --> 00:17.976
You? A boyfriend? Give me a break.

00:18.893 --> 00:20.895
Is that guy okay in the head?

00:20.979 --> 00:23.857
You've played him. He doesn't know
you're really just a gorilla.

00:23.940 --> 00:24.941
Excuse me?

00:25.025 --> 00:28.236
What the heck? Jealous much?

00:28.319 --> 00:31.948
Keep that up, and he'll catch on.
You'll end up getting dumped again.

00:32.032 --> 00:36.161
Talk to me when you've figured out
your own love life.

00:36.244 --> 00:38.371
Though, I doubt you can.

00:38.455 --> 00:39.664
What...

00:40.582 --> 00:41.583
Shut up.

00:45.879 --> 00:47.130
Hey, don't let it get to you.

00:47.213 --> 00:49.090
Know what? You irritate me.

00:49.674 --> 00:52.594
SORRY, LET'S BREAK UP

00:57.182 --> 01:00.602
WHY?

01:00.685 --> 01:02.604
WHAT DID I DO?

01:07.567 --> 01:09.110
He hasn't read my messages.

01:09.194 --> 01:10.528
Wait, did he block me?

01:12.197 --> 01:13.865
It's over.

01:16.659 --> 01:19.162
The end always comes
before it even begins.

01:19.871 --> 01:23.500
What did he like about me, to begin with?

01:23.583 --> 01:25.376
What did he know about me?

01:28.463 --> 01:33.468
Igarashi's only had eyes for Koyun...
Wish someone liked me like that too.

01:35.220 --> 01:38.807
Koyun, what do you find
so repulsive about Igarashi?

01:40.683 --> 01:43.645
Well, I mean,
there's a lot to dislike about him.

01:43.728 --> 01:46.314
But he's so into you.

01:46.397 --> 01:47.398
AZUMI

01:48.024 --> 01:49.943
Isn't being liked good enough?

01:50.026 --> 01:51.277
Asking for more is greedy.

01:52.904 --> 01:53.905
You're right.

01:54.572 --> 01:57.450
I should be grateful he likes me at all.

01:58.660 --> 02:04.040
Igarashi might be the only person
who will keep liking me.

02:04.666 --> 02:05.667
Koyun?

02:07.794 --> 02:10.213
Where to next? Karaoke?

02:10.296 --> 02:12.423
Let's see.

02:12.507 --> 02:15.552
Not long after, Koyun quit her club

02:15.635 --> 02:18.054
and started going out with Igarashi.

02:19.347 --> 02:22.433
Seriously, I shouldn't have said that.

02:23.101 --> 02:25.228
Isn't being liked good enough?

02:25.311 --> 02:26.646
Asking for more is greedy.

02:27.313 --> 02:30.692
Is it... all my fault?

03:56.361 --> 04:01.950
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

04:02.533 --> 04:06.955
EPISODE 6
NEW SEMESTER

04:09.916 --> 04:11.709
This year is almost over.

04:11.793 --> 04:12.794
AMAMIYA RESIDENCE
LIVING ROOM

04:12.877 --> 04:13.878
What's that all of a sudden?

04:13.962 --> 04:16.381
You're sad about
that one senior graduating, huh?

04:17.215 --> 04:19.050
Hey! That's not it!

04:19.133 --> 04:21.010
- You mean the one from the band?
- Yep.

04:21.094 --> 04:22.095
THIRD YEAR

04:22.178 --> 04:23.346
Wrong! You're dead wrong!

04:23.930 --> 04:24.973
Why don't you ask her out?

04:25.056 --> 04:26.432
Easy for you to say.

04:26.516 --> 04:30.311
You... You'll never understand how I feel!

04:30.812 --> 04:32.188
So you admit it, Hayato.

04:32.272 --> 04:33.856
What do you mean? I do too.

04:33.940 --> 04:35.483
No, you don't.

04:35.984 --> 04:38.653
You've never been in love before.

04:39.320 --> 04:40.738
That's rude.

04:40.822 --> 04:44.450
I've always loved my girlfriends
as much as they've loved me.

04:44.534 --> 04:46.703
- You're kinda like that!
- You're kinda like that!

04:46.786 --> 04:49.372
You're just neutral about everyone.

04:49.455 --> 04:50.999
But isn't that a good thing?

04:51.582 --> 04:53.042
Is it really so bad?

04:53.126 --> 04:54.127
It is.

04:54.210 --> 04:56.879
That's why you're always fine
after a break up.

04:56.963 --> 04:59.048
However I take it,

04:59.132 --> 05:03.386
the fact is,
they still wanted to break up, right?

05:03.469 --> 05:06.389
This is pointless, and I'm getting pissed.

05:06.973 --> 05:09.642
I hope one day,
you fall in love with someone

05:10.643 --> 05:12.603
who doesn't care about you at all.

05:12.687 --> 05:15.106
I hope she tramples all over your heart.

05:15.189 --> 05:16.190
That's right.

05:16.274 --> 05:17.900
We're friends, right?

05:18.484 --> 05:20.320
You hear that? Aren't they horrible?

05:23.865 --> 05:25.241
She laughed.

05:27.827 --> 05:28.995
How cute.

05:29.078 --> 05:30.997
STARE

05:35.543 --> 05:37.879
I'd never waste my time like that.

05:37.962 --> 05:39.255
- I figured.
- I figured.

05:41.424 --> 05:43.009
Emotions.

05:43.676 --> 05:47.013
The more you let it show,
the more it gets used against you.

05:51.100 --> 05:53.478
These guys don't hold back.

05:58.816 --> 06:01.277
It's never made sense to me.

06:01.861 --> 06:06.032
You tell me to set goals,
but you're against me chasing my dreams?

06:06.115 --> 06:08.951
Yours don't seem that serious.

06:09.035 --> 06:11.370
You just want to move out
and mess around all day.

06:11.454 --> 06:13.164
What's that? Say that again, bastard!

06:13.247 --> 06:14.749
- So noisy.
- Enough already!

06:14.832 --> 06:17.668
I wish he'd leave already,
that good-for-nothing punk.

06:18.795 --> 06:21.172
You let your emotions take over
and end up in an argument...

06:21.964 --> 06:25.426
What "feeling" makes someone go that far?

06:26.594 --> 06:29.472
Emotions are nothing
but your brain sending signals, right?

06:30.098 --> 06:32.391
You should be able to control them.

06:36.395 --> 06:37.563
Hey, hey!

06:41.150 --> 06:42.527
Hikawa.

06:49.117 --> 06:50.576
Sorry.

06:53.287 --> 06:55.706
No, no, no, no!

06:57.792 --> 06:59.460
Stop it, brain.

06:59.544 --> 07:02.213
Stop it. Stop!

07:02.296 --> 07:05.925
SOUND ASLEEP

07:06.008 --> 07:07.218
A sea slug?

07:07.301 --> 07:08.469
CLICK CLICK

07:08.553 --> 07:09.929
That's it, you look adorable.

07:10.012 --> 07:12.306
Over here? This angle? Yeah?

07:12.974 --> 07:14.559
ARE YOU FREE
THE DAY AFTER TOMORROW?

07:14.642 --> 07:15.643
It's Yota.

07:19.480 --> 07:21.566
SORRY, I GOT
CLUB ACTIVITIES ALL DAY

07:21.649 --> 07:22.900
GOTCHA

07:25.736 --> 07:26.737
Yota.

07:28.448 --> 07:30.158
Sorry, did I keep you waiting?

07:30.783 --> 07:31.784
Not in the slightest.

07:32.410 --> 07:34.245
You're really easy to spot.

07:34.996 --> 07:35.997
That's good.

07:36.998 --> 07:38.541
You're all puffy.

07:38.624 --> 07:40.334
And you're fluffy.

07:41.419 --> 07:43.129
Sorry to make you tag along.

07:43.212 --> 07:45.423
Don't be sorry. I wanted
to visit Miki at work too.

07:45.506 --> 07:46.799
EPISODE: OFF TO MIKI'S WORK!

07:46.883 --> 07:48.968
It's hard to stop by on your own.

07:49.844 --> 07:52.305
I marked the location on the map.

07:52.388 --> 07:54.056
Look at you, all prepared.

07:54.557 --> 07:56.142
Let's see.

07:56.225 --> 07:58.019
- Right this way.
- Thanks.

08:02.523 --> 08:03.649
Welcome...

08:03.733 --> 08:04.942
Hey, Koyun and Yota.

08:05.026 --> 08:07.612
OUT OF BREATH

08:07.695 --> 08:09.197
Did something happen?

08:09.280 --> 08:12.325
We were lost for 30 minutes.

08:12.408 --> 08:15.203
What? How come?
It's a five-minute walk from the station.

08:16.704 --> 08:18.623
I think you've got the wrong way.

08:18.706 --> 08:19.707
Say what?

08:20.583 --> 08:23.461
- Sorry I picked a weird time to come by.
- Thanks.

08:24.045 --> 08:26.297
I can't really talk
until the lunch rush is over.

08:26.797 --> 08:29.842
This is the most popular one,

08:29.926 --> 08:32.720
but I personally recommend
the one with avocado.

08:32.803 --> 08:34.972
Yota, you might like this one. It's spicy.

08:35.056 --> 08:37.183
- Then, I'll go with that one.
- That was quick.

08:37.683 --> 08:39.310
I need a minute.

08:39.393 --> 08:41.229
Take your time.

08:42.355 --> 08:45.024
- Then, I'll get the one with avocado.
- Okay.

08:45.525 --> 08:47.818
We have an order!
One chili and one avocado.

08:47.902 --> 08:49.153
Comin' right up.

08:49.237 --> 08:50.321
Miki.

08:51.697 --> 08:53.407
Are those two dating?

08:53.491 --> 08:57.245
What? As if. We're all just friends.

08:57.328 --> 08:58.371
Really?

08:58.454 --> 09:02.625
I mean, I think they look good together.

09:04.835 --> 09:08.005
The little one is next to the tall one.

09:08.089 --> 09:09.882
They're a perfect match, don't you think?

09:09.966 --> 09:11.884
How heartwarming.

09:11.968 --> 09:13.636
Yota and Koyun?

09:14.845 --> 09:17.598
Now that he mentioned it,
I've never considered it before.

09:18.099 --> 09:20.560
If they ended up together,

09:21.561 --> 09:23.104
what would I do?

09:25.273 --> 09:26.732
I'd totally ship them.

09:27.400 --> 09:29.193
Yes. They're a match made in heaven.

09:29.277 --> 09:31.988
Koyun would be better off
with someone like Yota...

09:33.364 --> 09:35.741
- No thanks.
- No, no, no, no, no, no!

09:36.576 --> 09:40.371
I need to learn
to stay out of people's business.

09:44.000 --> 09:45.751
How do I bite into this?

09:47.420 --> 09:49.380
How does it even fit in your mouth?

09:50.673 --> 09:51.591
AH

09:51.674 --> 09:52.592
PFFT

09:54.260 --> 09:56.095
What? What is it?

09:56.679 --> 09:59.682
Yes... I can just see them working out.

10:01.809 --> 10:03.102
I'm home.

10:04.103 --> 10:05.313
Welcome back.

10:05.396 --> 10:08.232
You're home. What about your job?

10:08.316 --> 10:09.734
I got off early today.

10:09.817 --> 10:13.529
Look. I took this pic of Ponta
lazing around like a sea slug.

10:13.613 --> 10:15.615
Aw, how precious.

10:16.240 --> 10:18.034
Send it to me too.

10:18.117 --> 10:19.243
Okay.

10:19.327 --> 10:21.871
Let's see, where's that chat with her...

10:22.455 --> 10:25.625
What's this? Yota updated his profile pic.

10:25.708 --> 10:26.876
That's rare.

10:27.877 --> 10:29.045
Why a burger?

10:31.213 --> 10:33.132
KOYUKI HIKAWA PROFILE UPDATED

10:33.215 --> 10:34.216
ACK

10:37.345 --> 10:39.138
What?

10:39.722 --> 10:41.932
Minato, have you sent the photo yet?

10:42.016 --> 10:43.392
What are you doing?

10:43.976 --> 10:47.063
What does it all mean?

10:53.861 --> 10:54.945
I knew it.

10:55.655 --> 10:57.406
Hikawa's got a crush on...

11:00.034 --> 11:01.869
GRADE 1 CLASS 6

11:01.952 --> 11:04.205
The winter break came and went in a flash.

11:04.288 --> 11:07.500
Yota, your profile pic...
What's up with that?

11:09.543 --> 11:10.544
Oh, that?

11:11.712 --> 11:12.713
NONCHALANT

11:12.797 --> 11:13.964
I'm matching with Koyun.

11:14.048 --> 11:15.049
Miki drew it.

11:15.549 --> 11:16.759
What? Miki?

11:17.802 --> 11:22.056
You see, the illustrations on the menu
were drawn by yours truly.

11:22.139 --> 11:24.517
- Wow, that's amazing!
- This one that's alive is cute.

11:24.600 --> 11:25.601
THE ONE THAT'S ALIVE

11:25.684 --> 11:27.770
Keep the compliments coming!

11:27.853 --> 11:30.648
We looked at it when Koyun and I
visited Miki at her work.

11:30.731 --> 11:31.732
CRACK

11:32.316 --> 11:33.651
Just the two of you?

11:33.734 --> 11:37.488
Yeah. I asked if you were free,
but you said you had practice all day.

11:38.823 --> 11:40.241
Now that you mention it...

11:41.450 --> 11:46.080
When making plans, it's considerate to let
people know what you're inviting them to.

11:47.331 --> 11:48.332
Yota.

11:50.251 --> 11:52.378
It hurts to be left out.

11:52.461 --> 11:55.089
You're unusually honest,
and it's creeping me out.

11:55.172 --> 11:56.632
That's harsh.

11:56.715 --> 11:57.716
GRADE 1 CLASS 2

11:57.800 --> 12:01.679
Lastly, we still haven't decided
the library committee member.

12:03.722 --> 12:06.851
Work made the winter break fly by.

12:07.893 --> 12:09.937
It was so boring.

12:10.020 --> 12:11.730
The shifts are flexible,

12:11.814 --> 12:13.399
the customers are chill,

12:13.482 --> 12:16.485
and hardly anyone my age comes in,
so it's the ideal job in a way.

12:16.569 --> 12:18.112
I hope they don't go out of business.

12:19.029 --> 12:22.741
Who here isn't
a part of a club or a committee?

12:32.460 --> 12:34.003
LIBRARY COMMITTEE MEMBERS (2)
HIKAWA - SHIMOJIMA

12:34.086 --> 12:36.005
HIKAWA - BAM

12:36.088 --> 12:38.507
LIBRARY REP RESPONSIBILITIES

12:38.591 --> 12:41.302
Sounded like we'll have our hands full.

12:41.385 --> 12:45.014
We have to stick around till school's out
when we're manning the desk.

12:45.097 --> 12:46.474
DEAD SILENT

12:47.266 --> 12:49.018
What an awkward silence.

12:51.228 --> 12:53.355
I'll have to adjust my work schedule.

12:55.774 --> 12:58.903
A thought just occurred to me.
You're not in any clubs either, right?

12:58.986 --> 12:59.987
FLUSTERED

13:00.070 --> 13:01.655
No, I'm in art club.

13:01.739 --> 13:06.494
We draw freely, so people tend
to think we have it easy. There's that.

13:06.577 --> 13:08.537
FLUSTERED THAT KOYUN
SUDDENLY MADE CONVERSATION

13:10.122 --> 13:13.876
The sports clubs must think
we've got all the time in the world.

13:13.959 --> 13:15.711
That's what they think of us.

13:15.794 --> 13:16.795
PISSED OFF

13:16.879 --> 13:17.922
STARE

13:18.005 --> 13:19.798
Oh, no!
Did I sound like I was complaining?

13:21.091 --> 13:22.384
That's irritating.

13:23.511 --> 13:26.639
I hate people who make assumptions
and look down on others.

13:28.224 --> 13:31.352
I thought this school
didn't really have that problem.

13:31.977 --> 13:34.146
Wait, what? Did she just...

13:35.231 --> 13:36.232
try to relate to me?

13:38.651 --> 13:39.652
That's...

13:41.320 --> 13:42.321
Sorry.

13:42.905 --> 13:44.406
I'm going that way for a bit.

13:45.074 --> 13:46.075
Sure.

13:46.659 --> 13:47.660
Catch you later.

13:48.953 --> 13:50.454
Yeah, see you.

13:51.497 --> 13:55.084
Hikawa wasn't as scary as I thought.

13:58.003 --> 13:59.004
Yota.

13:59.964 --> 14:00.965
Koyun.

14:04.552 --> 14:06.262
- Happy New Year.
- Happy New Year.

14:11.183 --> 14:12.726
What about your club activities, Yota?

14:13.310 --> 14:14.353
No club today.

14:14.436 --> 14:15.896
The gym is in use.

14:16.397 --> 14:17.398
I see.

14:18.148 --> 14:20.985
- Have you been out here all this time?
- Yeah.

14:21.652 --> 14:25.698
I like to gaze up at the sky
absent-mindedly like this.

14:26.407 --> 14:27.491
Really?

14:27.992 --> 14:30.202
Is there something on your mind?

14:30.703 --> 14:32.121
No, not really.

14:33.330 --> 14:35.082
I don't think about anything.

14:38.460 --> 14:39.461
I see.

14:42.631 --> 14:43.632
This is peaceful.

14:44.592 --> 14:47.761
Both the time drifting by slowly
and Yota too.

14:49.096 --> 14:52.725
Time flows slowly,
as if he's a drifting cloud.

14:54.643 --> 14:57.104
"Yota" means "the sun,"
but he's more like a cloud.

14:57.187 --> 14:58.188
CHUCKLE

14:59.231 --> 15:01.567
Not thinking about anything is hard.

15:03.819 --> 15:07.239
Thoughts are constantly
running through my head.

15:07.740 --> 15:10.701
The smallest things make me overthink,
and I get worked up over them.

15:11.201 --> 15:13.370
I get tired of myself for that.

15:15.664 --> 15:17.374
Yota and I are polar opposites.

15:19.627 --> 15:22.838
I can't imagine Yota
getting hung up over the little things

15:22.922 --> 15:25.883
or worrying about them like I do.

15:28.844 --> 15:29.929
It must be nice.

15:31.347 --> 15:33.057
I want to be like him.

15:39.563 --> 15:42.399
Hey, Amamiya, stop getting distracted!

15:42.900 --> 15:45.235
Is this... actually happening?

15:54.453 --> 15:56.455
I read from start to finish.

15:57.331 --> 15:59.541
There are less visitors
than I anticipated.

16:01.293 --> 16:02.294
Is that an art book?

16:02.378 --> 16:05.339
Yeah. Looking at it helps me learn.

16:06.090 --> 16:08.592
You're a great artist, Shimojima.

16:08.676 --> 16:10.260
I'm really not...

16:10.344 --> 16:12.888
Hold on, you've seen my drawings before?

16:12.972 --> 16:14.264
Oh, yeah.

16:14.348 --> 16:18.227
When we were doing oil paintings,
I could see your canvas from my spot.

16:19.603 --> 16:21.522
Sorry to peek without asking.

16:21.605 --> 16:22.940
SCURRYING AWAY
EMOTIONAL DISTANCE

16:23.023 --> 16:25.275
What? Don't worry about it. Come back.

16:28.362 --> 16:30.531
- See you later.
- See you tomorrow.

16:33.450 --> 16:36.328
Maybe I should look at some art books too.

16:36.412 --> 16:38.288
I wonder what art book
I should start with.

16:38.372 --> 16:40.290
GROWL

16:47.256 --> 16:48.841
His head is sticking out.

16:50.718 --> 16:52.052
CLEARLY YOTA

16:53.679 --> 16:54.680
THUD

16:54.763 --> 16:56.348
I'm sorry.

16:56.432 --> 16:57.850
It's you, Koyun.

16:57.933 --> 16:59.476
You scared me.

17:01.395 --> 17:05.107
Geez, it's dangerous
if you get in my blind spot.

17:05.190 --> 17:07.317
You make it sound like you're a truck.

17:07.985 --> 17:09.695
What are you buying, Koyun?

17:09.778 --> 17:13.615
- I'm a little hungry. Anything will do.
- Same here.

17:13.699 --> 17:15.200
FREE GIFT WITH A HOT SNACK
CHECK YOUR RECEIPT

17:15.284 --> 17:17.453
Are you in a hurry to get home, Koyun?

17:22.791 --> 17:24.543
This is warming my hands up.

17:26.045 --> 17:27.921
It's gonna get cold.

17:28.005 --> 17:31.008
What about dinner at your house, Yota?
Is that okay?

17:31.091 --> 17:32.468
Of course, it's okay.

17:34.887 --> 17:37.139
- I can eat it all easily.
- That figures.

17:37.222 --> 17:38.223
SECOND ONE

17:39.016 --> 17:42.436
You've been staying late
at school recently.

17:42.519 --> 17:45.272
I'm on library duty right now.

17:45.355 --> 17:47.775
Did they force it on you?

17:48.484 --> 17:50.486
No, that's not what it is.

17:51.779 --> 17:53.864
Come to think of it, is that what it is?

17:56.075 --> 18:00.162
But I've become interested in things
I never thought I'd look at before.

18:00.245 --> 18:02.581
So it's not that bad. So far.

18:03.165 --> 18:05.084
I have a lot of time to space out.

18:05.167 --> 18:06.627
Really?

18:06.710 --> 18:08.754
I should've done it too.

18:09.338 --> 18:12.174
You don't have time for that
with your club activities.

18:14.593 --> 18:17.805
But I want to spend some time zoning out.

18:20.516 --> 18:24.394
Talking with Yota makes me feel at ease.

18:26.980 --> 18:27.981
It feels warm.

18:36.073 --> 18:38.408
The fries aren't salty enough today.

18:38.492 --> 18:40.786
Hikawa and Yota...

18:45.082 --> 18:46.583
I wish they wouldn't...

18:49.753 --> 18:53.841
Even if you fall in love with Yota,
you'll just end up suffering.

18:59.721 --> 19:01.557
Yota, is your house that way?

19:01.640 --> 19:04.560
Yeah. But I'll walk you to the station.

19:04.643 --> 19:05.811
You don't have to.

19:05.894 --> 19:09.106
But I'm worried you'll get lost.

19:09.189 --> 19:10.357
I won't get lost.

19:13.402 --> 19:14.528
Yota!

19:18.991 --> 19:21.034
That scared me.

19:21.118 --> 19:23.495
Turn on your lights. Geez.

19:26.498 --> 19:27.499
SHE SLID

19:27.583 --> 19:29.001
Are you okay?

19:29.084 --> 19:30.878
Yeah. Sorry.

19:31.545 --> 19:33.130
Here, hold on to me.

19:33.714 --> 19:34.798
There you go.

19:47.477 --> 19:48.478
Is something wrong?

19:49.771 --> 19:50.856
No.

19:51.857 --> 19:52.858
Just now...

19:54.359 --> 19:56.445
When I was small...

19:57.529 --> 20:00.199
I just suddenly remembered my dad.

20:01.408 --> 20:02.701
It felt floaty.

20:02.784 --> 20:03.827
FLOATY

20:03.911 --> 20:06.205
Wait, what am I even explaining?

20:08.457 --> 20:10.876
It's okay.
You can call me the wrong name sometimes.

20:10.959 --> 20:13.837
That's what elementary school kids do
to their teachers.

20:17.758 --> 20:18.842
I see.

20:19.676 --> 20:20.677
That's why.

20:22.804 --> 20:25.349
I wonder how my dad is doing.

20:30.312 --> 20:31.772
If you were my daughter,

20:31.855 --> 20:34.566
I'd have to go to the Lost Child Center
every time we went out.

20:34.650 --> 20:37.361
I told you I wouldn't get lost every time.

20:39.821 --> 20:40.822
Yota?

20:49.831 --> 20:51.041
What are you doing here?

20:51.833 --> 20:53.585
I forgot to buy a lot of things.

20:54.670 --> 20:56.505
What about Haruto and Sakura?

20:57.631 --> 20:59.007
Dad's at home.

20:59.091 --> 21:01.426
He's already back home today.

21:01.510 --> 21:03.845
- Did you need dinner today at all?
- A family member?

21:03.929 --> 21:06.515
- Yes, I do. Sorry I didn't contact you.
- Is she his sister?

21:06.598 --> 21:09.810
Maybe I should go home.

21:09.893 --> 21:11.061
Yota.

21:11.144 --> 21:14.648
Well, I'll be back soon after I walk
my friend to the station.

21:16.942 --> 21:18.110
Okay.

21:18.610 --> 21:19.861
Be careful out there.

21:32.499 --> 21:34.501
Yota, was that okay?

21:35.794 --> 21:37.963
Well...

21:38.880 --> 21:40.173
- Your sister--
- My mom.

21:43.468 --> 21:46.305
She's my mother.

21:46.388 --> 21:50.183
?? YEARS OLD - 16 YEARS OLD = ??

21:50.267 --> 21:51.560
What?

21:52.144 --> 21:53.937
We're not related by blood though.

21:55.230 --> 21:58.859
My real mother died
when I was in elementary school.

22:06.199 --> 22:08.869
Oh, sorry.
I guess that's a natural reaction.

22:08.952 --> 22:10.203
Oh, no...

22:11.330 --> 22:13.957
It's been a while, so I'm fine.

22:14.791 --> 22:15.917
Right now,

22:17.002 --> 22:18.712
the family I have
is what feels normal to me.

23:50.262 --> 23:55.267
Subtitle translation by Megumi Hunter
